# .cursorrules
rules:
  - id: security-owasp-top10
    description: >
      Enforce OWASP Top 10 secure coding practices across the backend (FastAPI)
      and frontend (React) to minimize security risks such as injection,
      broken authentication, and data exposure.
    applies_to:
      - backend/**/*.py
      - frontend/**/*.js
      - frontend/**/*.tsx
    guidance:
      - Input validation and sanitization required for all user-supplied data.
      - Always use parameterized queries or ORM-safe methods (no string SQL).
      - Never trust client input; validate types and ranges on server.
      - Escape all output rendered into HTML or templates.
      - Enforce authentication for all protected endpoints.
      - Use JWTs or session cookies with HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=strict.
      - Store secrets in environment variables, not code.
      - Use HTTPS-only cookies and enforce TLS in all API calls.
      - Avoid exposing stack traces or internal errors to users.
      - Implement proper CORS restrictions (no wildcard domains in production).
      - Apply rate limiting and CSRF protection where applicable.
      - Verify dependencies regularly with `npm audit` / `pip audit`.
      - Use role-based access control (RBAC) for sensitive actions.
      - Log authentication and authorization events securely (no PII).
      - Ensure error messages do not leak sensitive data.
      - Enforce strong password hashing (bcrypt/argon2).
      - Avoid localStorage for auth tokens (use cookies or memory store).
      - Sanitize all file uploads and validate MIME types.
      - Validate redirect URLs to prevent open redirects.
      - Implement content security policy (CSP) in frontend headers.
    on_violation:
      - warn
      - explain why it’s insecure
      - suggest the OWASP category and fix
categories:
  - A01:2021 Broken Access Control
  - A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures
  - A03:2021 Injection
  - A04:2021 Insecure Design
  - A05:2021 Security Misconfiguration
  - A07:2021 Identification and Authentication Failures
  - A08:2021 Software and Data Integrity Failures
